WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.810
The artist returns to the
copper centrepiece and

00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:05.810
begins to weave,
starting with rattan

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:08.060
reeds that have also
soaked to make them more

00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:11.300
pliable. She pulls the
reeds through the tabs

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:13.700
and inner crosses them
so that they fan out in

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:14.930
two directions.

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:18.050
She then braids cotton
string against the

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:20.990
centerpiece. This
creates a neat and sturdy

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:25.880
border all the way
around. She then trims

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:27.500
the ends of the strings.

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:35.420
Next, the artist weaves
rattan reeds parallel to

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:37.850
the cotton braid and
twining them with the

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:41.150
reeds that extend
outward. She creates one

00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:43.670
row of these rigid
fibers for structure.

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:48.140
She's now ready for the
palm strands after the

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:51.050
soaking. The strands
remain soft and pliable

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.870
for many hours, so she
doesn't have to rush the

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:54.560
work.

